WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.280
- [Narrator] Everyone around
here thinks they're a big man.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.363
Everyone wants to be a top boy.

00:00:08.936 --> 00:00:11.686
(dramatic music)

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.013
- [Narrator] I know London,

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.910
people pay a lot of money to get high.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.163
Dark, white, weed, all of that.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:27.880
Do you get me?

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.130
- When we did Top Boy before, it had huge

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.322
critical acclaim, it was loved.

00:00:33.322 --> 00:00:35.590
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.610
- When Top Boy seasons
one and two came out,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.750
I was in school.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.969
- Absolutely fell in love with it.

00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:42.290
- It's something that everyone watches.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.750
- You go in to school the
next day and it's like,

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.997
"Aw, did you watch last
night's episode of Top Boy?"

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:52.098
(upbeat music)

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.540
- As a writer, you learn to kind of roll

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.420
with the blows a bit,

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.266
if a show doesn't get made,
or a show gets canceled

00:01:00.266 --> 00:01:02.130
you shrug and you move onto the next one.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.090
But I felt really bad about this one.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.170
- I can't even put
petrol in the car without

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.623
someone saying, "yo, are
you gonna do a third one?"

00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:11.683
And it's just like "oh my god!"

00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:13.683
(music)

00:01:16.347 --> 00:01:19.187
- For years, I just remember
like watching television

00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:20.990
and whatever and watching shows

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.850
and not seeing yourself, do
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.790
Maybe when a person of color was on the TV

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.830
you'd scream upstairs like,
"Yo, someone's on TV! Like yo!"

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.390
Everyone run downstairs,
watch that character,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.281
see what they're saying.

00:01:33.281 --> 00:01:35.281
(music)

00:01:38.378 --> 00:01:39.350
- [Kane 'Kano' Robinson]
He was a fan of the show

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.570
when it first came out
and was public about that,

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.060
posting it on his social media.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.810
- [Ronan Bennett] He was just magnificent,

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.506
he loved the show, he just
wanted to do whatever he could.

00:01:48.506 --> 00:01:49.339
- [Kane 'Kano' Robinson]
Didn't really seem like

00:01:49.339 --> 00:01:51.740
no ego about it, it wasn't
about what this show

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.950
can do for me, it was
about like how could I

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.650
how could I help assist this show.

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:02.087
(music)

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.800
- He also did the bulk
of the pitch to Netflix

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.800
and I hardly had to say anything,

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:12.290
and that was fantastic.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.220
- [Drake] I just want to
express how happy this room

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.540
makes me right here, you know.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.140
The show meant the world
to me, I wish you the best.

00:02:19.274 --> 00:02:22.357
(noise from a crowd)

00:02:29.238 --> 00:02:31.238
(music)

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.453
- Ronan's writing set
the pace and it's kind of

00:02:37.453 --> 00:02:40.283
a continuation of his style I suppose.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.270
So what we're gonna do is create a show,

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.770
essentially the same show that
we would have created before,

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.500
but it's now in a climate where

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.740
everyone is gonna be able to consume it.

00:02:51.522 --> 00:02:53.522
(music)

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:16.520
- [Ashley Walters] Dushane
engineers a situation to get him

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.890
back on top, kind of
touching down in London

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.160
he realizes everything's changed.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.297
The youngers have become the olders,

00:03:24.297 --> 00:03:25.970
the youngers have got younger,

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.570
and it's just a different world.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.070
(music)

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:37.070
- It's all about Jamie when
Dushane comes back, he's no one.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.320
- [Narrator] Things have changed,

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.337
I'm running the first line.

00:03:41.337 --> 00:03:43.337
(music)

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.450
- [Ronan Bennett] We
didn't go out to stars,

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.040
a very high proportion of our actors

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.653
are first time actors,
from similar backgrounds.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:16.210
- [Narrator] The criteria
is, do they feel authentic?

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:18.007
Do we believe they come
from those streets?

00:04:18.007 --> 00:04:20.450
- [Ashley 'Bashy' Thomas] I
have family members and friends

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.830
come from this world
and a lot of the people

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.620
who are in the production
grew up around that world,

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.240
so we've got a
responsibility to tell these

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.370
stories authentically.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.770
- Acting for people where
I'm from doesn't feel like

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.640
a real thing and it never actually clicked

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.110
that you can go out and
do this type of thing

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.433
until like I saw people
really breaking down barriers.

00:04:43.557 --> 00:04:45.060
(music)

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.250
- [Ashley Walters] We're
shooting at the places where

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.430
this stuff goes down, we
were filming on a estate

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.000
where you know the local
guys that were dealing

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.720
couldn't deal because we were shooting,

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:58.227
so they're were asking
like, "we need money".

00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:01.809
(music)

00:05:15.115 --> 00:05:16.970
- [David 'Dave' Omoregie]
Top Boy is the most genuine,

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.280
raw depiction of life in
South, East, West, North London

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:24.260
so to be a part of it,
it feels like you're

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.730
being able to tell a story
as to where you come from

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:30.020
and what people go through, how life is.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.110
- It has to be as real
as possible, I feel,

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.050
that's why people love this so much,

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.350
because it was so real.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.475
- [Ashley Walters] You know
the vibe is nothing but 100%

00:05:37.475 --> 00:05:39.193
authenticity.

00:05:39.193 --> 00:05:41.193
(music)

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.490
- [Charles Steel] Its
strength is it dealing with

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:49.110
universal themes, you know,
about family ambition,

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.380
where we sit in the world,
it thrills and exciting,

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.180
but it has huge heart and humanity

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.180
and it's about people.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.210
- [Alasdair Flind] What this
is, both a rebirth and a new

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.280
start because we're making
this season for an audience

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.530
that's never seen Top Boy,

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:04.940
and we're also making it for
the core fans, who love the

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.530
show and are familiar with it.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.050
- [Narrator] I'm confident
that this is gonna

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.970
be like amazing man.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.280
- It's an explosion man,
it's gonna be seamless,

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.323
it's Top Boy, but just
Top Boy at its greatest.

00:06:17.532 --> 00:06:19.532
(music)

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.940
- [Narrator] If we do
this, we're back on top.

00:06:25.036 --> 00:06:26.540
What you saying?

